WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.633
Asking for Leave and Setting Boundaries.

2
00:00:02.913 --> 00:00:07.051
Day 75 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the Workplace phase.

3
00:00:08.801 --> 00:00:09.825
The key idea.

4
00:00:10.105 --> 00:00:12.367
Rested engineers write better code.

5
00:00:12.647 --> 00:00:16.721
Asking for leave and protecting your time are part of being a professional.

6
00:00:17.001 --> 00:00:20.201
Plan ahead, cover your work, and say it clearly without guilt.

7
00:00:21.551 --> 00:00:22.405
Part 1.

8
00:00:22.685 --> 00:00:24.093
Asking for planned leave.

9
00:00:25.343 --> 00:00:26.260
Step 1:

10
00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:29.591
Check: team calendar, release dates, on-call rota.

11
00:00:29.871 --> 00:00:30.788
Step 2:

12
00:00:31.068 --> 00:00:32.007
Ask early:

13
00:00:32.287 --> 00:00:35.465
2 to 4 weeks ahead for a week off; more for long leave.

14
00:00:35.745 --> 00:00:36.663
Step 3:

15
00:00:36.943 --> 00:00:39.375
Plan cover: who handles what while you're away.

16
00:00:39.655 --> 00:00:40.615
Step 4:

17
00:00:40.895 --> 00:00:44.905
Confirm in writing: leave system + calendar + team channel.

18
00:00:45.185 --> 00:00:46.145
Step 5:

19
00:00:46.425 --> 00:00:49.540
Hand over: notes before you go; out-of-office on.

20
00:00:50.890 --> 00:00:52.127
Asking your manager.

21
00:00:52.407 --> 00:00:53.346
You could say:

22
00:00:53.626 --> 00:00:57.957
I'd like to take leave from 15th to 22nd December for a family trip.

23
00:00:58.237 --> 00:01:02.546
I've checked: it's after the release, and Ravi can cover my on-call shift.

24
00:01:02.826 --> 00:01:06.218
I'll finish the search work and hand over notes before I go.

25
00:01:06.498 --> 00:01:07.778
Does that work for you?

26
00:01:09.128 --> 00:01:10.173
Note the wording:

27
00:01:10.453 --> 00:01:13.547
I'd like to take, not Can I please, if it's okay, maybe...

28
00:01:14.897 --> 00:01:16.305
Sick leave (same day).

29
00:01:16.585 --> 00:01:18.462
Here is a template you can copy.

30
00:01:18.742 --> 00:01:22.326
Hi Priya, I'm unwell today (fever) and won't be able to work.

31
00:01:22.606 --> 00:01:23.843
I'll take sick leave.

32
00:01:24.123 --> 00:01:25.211
Urgent items:

33
00:01:25.491 --> 00:01:29.523
PR 231 needs a review, Meena, could you take it?

34
00:01:29.803 --> 00:01:31.574
I'll update you tomorrow morning.

35
00:01:34.424 --> 00:01:35.469
Short and clear.

36
00:01:35.749 --> 00:01:37.797
You don't need to give medical details.

37
00:01:39.147 --> 00:01:40.321
Emergency leave.

38
00:01:40.601 --> 00:01:42.478
Here is a template you can copy.

39
00:01:42.758 --> 00:01:46.833
Hi Priya, I have a family emergency and need to leave right away.

40
00:01:47.113 --> 00:01:50.590
I'll be offline for. the rest of today, possibly tomorrow.

41
00:01:50.870 --> 00:01:52.982
Ravi has context on the cart bug.

42
00:01:53.262 --> 00:01:55.097
I'll update you as soon as I can.

43
00:01:57.947 --> 00:02:00.251
Long leave (wedding, parental, medical).

44
00:02:00.531 --> 00:02:01.469
You could say:

45
00:02:01.749 --> 00:02:03.499
I wanted to give you early notice:

46
00:02:03.779 --> 00:02:06.595
I'm planning parental leave from March for 3 months.

47
00:02:06.875 --> 00:02:08.816
I'd like to plan the handover together.

48
00:02:09.096 --> 00:02:12.147
Could we put together a coverage plan over the next few weeks?

49
00:02:13.497 --> 00:02:14.371
Part 2.

50
00:02:14.651 --> 00:02:16.017
Out-of-office message.

51
00:02:17.267 --> 00:02:19.144
Here is a template you can copy.

52
00:02:19.424 --> 00:02:20.768
Thanks for your message.

53
00:02:21.048 --> 00:02:25.400
I'm on leave from 15 to 22 Dec with limited access to email.

54
00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:30.843
For urgent checkout issues, please contact Ravi Kumar (ravi@example.com).

55
00:02:31.123 --> 00:02:35.069
For everything else, I'll reply after I return on 23 Dec.

56
00:02:37.919 --> 00:02:38.815
Part 3.

57
00:02:39.095 --> 00:02:40.695
Handover note before leave.

58
00:02:41.945 --> 00:02:43.823
Here is a template you can copy.

59
00:02:44.103 --> 00:02:47.153
Leave handover, Ashish (15 to 22 Dec).

60
00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:53.023
Search filters: merged; feature flag OFF, Meena to enable after QA sign-off.

61
00:02:53.303 --> 00:02:59.937
Bug 341: root cause found, fix in PR 245, needs one more review.

62
00:03:00.217 --> 00:03:03.247
On-call: swapped with Ravi (15 to 18 Dec).

63
00:03:03.527 --> 00:03:09.884
Don't panic if: nightly report job warns about latency, known issue, ticket 350.

64
00:03:12.734 --> 00:03:13.651
Part 4.

65
00:03:13.931 --> 00:03:15.147
Setting boundaries.

66
00:03:16.397 --> 00:03:18.957
Saying no to after-hours work (politely).

67
00:03:19.237 --> 00:03:20.645
Late-evening request.

68
00:03:20.925 --> 00:03:21.864
You could say:

69
00:03:22.144 --> 00:03:23.616
I'm logging off for the day.

70
00:03:23.896 --> 00:03:26.797
I'll pick this up first thing at 9:30 tomorrow.

71
00:03:27.077 --> 00:03:30.213
If it's a production issue, the on-call engineer is Meena.

72
00:03:31.563 --> 00:03:32.801
Weekend messages.

73
00:03:33.081 --> 00:03:34.019
You could say:

74
00:03:34.299 --> 00:03:36.219
(Monday) Saw your weekend message.

75
00:03:36.499 --> 00:03:38.206
I'll have it done by noon today.

76
00:03:38.486 --> 00:03:46.721
Going forward, if something is urgent on a weekend, a call is the best way to reach me, so I don't miss it, and I can switch off when it's not.

77
00:03:48.071 --> 00:03:49.137
Too many meetings.

78
00:03:49.417 --> 00:03:50.356
You could say:

79
00:03:50.636 --> 00:03:54.369
I'm in meetings 5 to 6 hours a day, and coding work is slipping.

80
00:03:54.649 --> 00:04:00.239
Could I block 10 am, 1 pm as focus time, and drop the meetings where I'm optional?

81
00:04:01.589 --> 00:04:03.146
Being pulled into everything.

82
00:04:03.426 --> 00:04:04.365
You could say:

83
00:04:04.645 --> 00:04:08.058
I'm happy to help, but if I take this, the search release slips.

84
00:04:08.338 --> 00:04:11.154
Can we check with Priya which one is the priority?

85
00:04:12.504 --> 00:04:13.635
Boundary habits.

86
00:04:13.915 --> 00:04:16.816
Set working hours in Slack or Teams and calendar.

87
00:04:17.096 --> 00:04:20.467
Turn off notifications after hours (except on-call).

88
00:04:20.747 --> 00:04:25.227
Schedule-send late-night messages for the morning so others don't feel pressure.

89
00:04:25.507 --> 00:04:28.195
Block focus time on your calendar, and protect it.

90
00:04:28.475 --> 00:04:31.867
Say Let me check my calendar before agreeing to anything big.

91
00:04:33.217 --> 00:04:33.857
Tip:

92
00:04:34.137 --> 00:04:35.417
Boundaries for leads.

93
00:04:35.697 --> 00:04:37.382
Your behaviour sets the norm.

94
00:04:37.662 --> 00:04:41.459
If you message at midnight, your team thinks they must answer at midnight.

95
00:04:41.739 --> 00:04:44.641
Use schedule-send, and take your own leave visibly.

96
00:04:45.991 --> 00:04:46.951
Part 5.

97
00:04:47.231 --> 00:04:48.617
Practice conversation:

98
00:04:48.897 --> 00:04:50.049
Asking for leave.

99
00:04:51.299 --> 00:04:53.326
Here is how the conversation goes.

100
00:04:53.606 --> 00:04:58.875
I'd like to take leave from the 15th to the 22nd of December for a family trip.

101
00:04:59.155 --> 00:05:01.182
That's right after the release, isn't it?

102
00:05:01.462 --> 00:05:03.531
Yes, the release is on the 12th.

103
00:05:03.811 --> 00:05:06.435
Ravi has agreed to cover my on-call shift.

104
00:05:06.715 --> 00:05:08.251
What about the search work?

105
00:05:09.601 --> 00:05:11.201
The conversation continues.

106
00:05:11.481 --> 00:05:14.724
I'll finish it before I go and write a handover note.

107
00:05:15.004 --> 00:05:16.092
Sounds good.

108
00:05:16.372 --> 00:05:17.268
Approved.

109
00:05:17.548 --> 00:05:18.828
Enjoy your trip!

110
00:05:19.108 --> 00:05:20.025
Thank you!

111
00:05:21.375 --> 00:05:22.911
That's the end of this lesson.

112
00:05:23.191 --> 00:05:27.863
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

113
00:05:28.143 --> 00:05:34.245
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

